I won't defend VAXnotes; I'm strongly critical of it not having been 
enhanced during the past few years in spite of numerous "wish lists" that 
were created, and I assume, given to DEC. Besides giving it a low 
priority, maybe DEC feels that it is "stable" and shouldn't be monkeyed  
with.

But, there is a public domain tpu utility written by the folks at DECUSERVE 
(home of the best VAXnotes system in the world) called ONEKEY, that makes 
using Notes easier via keypad commands. A separate module, called from 
within ONEKEY, will allow you to perform a global search of keywords in 
titles. These utilities are public domain - I don't know if they are in the 
DECUS tapes/files, but are available on the DECUSERVE system.

Mike



