At a small Digital research site where I used to work in an earlier
life, we stored all information possible in two large VAXnotes files.
Everyone worked with it, manager to secretary, chief engineer to
students. You had to :-) since it was our main archive anyway, and it
replaced the mailing lists ALL-IN-1 users are so fond of :-(  .

The problem of throwing out expired notes was "solved" by writing a DCL
proc that scanned the whole conference for topics/replies with the
keyword EXPIRATION=(date) and deleted the appropriate notes. This was
workable since everyone stored notes with an expiration date attached to
it. The proc ran in the batch queue, of course.

Other very valuable additions were also implemented in a DCL proc, and
basically got all new notes of remote VAXnotes to your local system so
you didn't have to wait minutes to get to the other end of the globe.
But, since most DECnet networks are not spanning the globe, this proc
might be of less use to you :-)


Jeroen



