On our campus NNTP-based News have superseded VMS-NOTES. Reasons:

	1) Price.
		NNTP-servers are more or less free. (B-News and C-News)
		and run on any cheap UNIX-box (yes: read PC)

		News readers are free. (GNUS, xrn, rn)
		

	2) Versatility.
		NNTP-based news readers often allow multiple servers,
		this allows burden sharing.

		NNTP-based news readers are available even for VMS, 
		but "NOTES" are not available for non-VMS systems.
			

best, adams


