PC software.  Is the problem that companies expect to pay for site licenses well 
below what an individual would pay retail from a computer store or mail order 
house?  Or that they don't look at per user costs this way?  Or that purchasing 
bureaucracy is such that it's easier to buy 800 copies at $38/piece than one
copy at $30K?  Or that they only expect a handful of people to actually use it? 
Or that most software for departmental systems (as opposed to PC's) is priced
differently?

Or maybe I'm just missing something obvious.

